addons/hdr: differential harness for the HDR/RGBE/EXR/UltraHDR/HDRCubeTexture loaders
(src/addons/loaders) and fflate's unzlibSync (src/addons/libs) against upstream.

  node diff/run_all.mjs --only hdr     the checks below (corrupt full run with --full)

  node fflate_diff.mjs N   unzlibSync vs fflate.module.js: N random streams (node zlib at
                           every level/strategy/window, fflate's zlibSync), 3N corrupt ones
                           (truncation, bit flips, random bytes, FDICT bit), the 951 zlib
                           chunks of the ZIP/ZIPS/PXR24 EXRs, and the out/dictionary options;
                           compares bytes, buffer layout and thrown message/code
  node run.mjs [--only hdr,exr,cube,ultra] [--filter re] [--verbose]
                           real load() on both sides (mock fetch), comparing texture fields,
                           image size, data hash, texData incl. header objects; every .hdr
                           and .exr of upstream examples/ plus the 415 generated EXRs
  node corrupt_run.mjs [--every N] [--limit-ms 15000]
                           truncated/corrupted HDR and EXR files (2251, derived by the script
                           and written to OUT/addons_hdr/corrupt), one process per load so a
                           non-terminating upstream parse is compared by its stack
  node probe_hangs.mjs     finds the EXRs upstream's parse never finishes on (both sides);
                           compares with hangs.json, which run.mjs reads to skip them
  node gen_exr.mjs         regenerates the EXR fixtures (see below)
  node tiny.mjs            prints the tiny fixtures of the loaders' MoonBit unit tests
                           (needs exrmetrics)
  python3 inject.py [bug]  bug injection on the real src files (each bug applied, mod/
                           rebuilt, the catching check run, file restored); 33 bugs

Fixtures. The 415 EXRs live in OUT/addons_hdr/exr (default diff/.out, gitignored) and are
unpacked automatically by fixtures.mjs (node gen_exr.mjs, about a second) from the
committed fixtures/exr.tar.xz (2.4 MB) when missing or stale. They were generated by
`node gen_exr.mjs --openexr`:
  - 78 are written by gen_exr.mjs in Node (scanline none/rle/zips/zip bases, deep, a
    multi-part file) and gen_dwa_deflate.mjs (2 DWA files rewritten to DEFLATE AC data);
  - 337 are written by OpenEXR's CLI from those bases (every compression and pixel mode by
    `exrmetrics --convert`, tiled/mipmapped/ripmapped by `exrmaketiled`, multi-part by
    `exrmultipart -combine`).
All 415 are in the archive, so no OpenEXR install is needed (CI has none), and the
Node-written ones too: their ZIP/ZIPS chunks come from node:zlib, whose output differs
between Node versions (Node 22 stores 15 fewer chunks compressed than Node 25.8, which
made the archive, and hdr_fflate counts those chunks: 2616 instead of 2631).
To regenerate the archive (after changing gen_exr.mjs): install OpenEXR >= 3.3
(`brew install openexr`; exrmetrics is new in 3.3, Ubuntu 24.04's 3.1 lacks it), then
`node gen_exr.mjs --openexr --pack`, and update the expected counts if they change.
With OpenEXR 3.4.4 and Node 25.8 the output is byte-identical to the archive.
The corrupt inputs are always derived by corrupt_run.mjs.

mod/ is a module (moon.work: mod/ and the repository root) with one package, harness,
exporting the functions run.mjs, case.mjs and one.mjs call; it imports the real
moonbit-community/three/addons/{loaders,libs}. The loaders' own unit tests run with the repo's
`moon test`, not here.

UltraHDR stubs (env.mjs installUltra): createImageBitmap reads the JPEG SOF size and fills
pixels from a hash of the bytes, a 2D canvas scales nearest-neighbour, DOMParser is a small
tag/attribute matcher; both sides use the same objects. ultra_synth.mjs builds ISO 21496-1,
XMP-variant and failure containers.
